; A negative base with an integer exponent: `pow64`'s `checkint` selects the
; sign host-independently (odd exponent -> negative via sign_bias, even ->
; positive). A non-integer exponent on a negative base is NaN — covered by the
; inline IEEE-754 matrix in `trig.zig`, not pinnable as a finite `{d}`. Pinned
; decimals are the canonical `{d}` rendering.
(pow -2.0 3.0)
(pow -2.0 2.0)
